# Spellbook Vendor (a 2/2): "At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may pay {1}. When you do, create a Sorcerer Role token
# attached to target creature you control." Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Vendor (combat comes with no Plains untapped: it can't pay, so
# nothing is asked). On turn 3 it pays {1} with its Plains and, when it does, Bot2's Ornithopter is refused as the target and
# the Role goes on its own Memnite (2/2). On turn 5 it declines: no second Role.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Spellbook Vendor
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spellbook Vendor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.PayCost
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Toughness = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Spellbook Vendor.Power = 2
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
[T5 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Spellbook Vendor.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
